From 7e0d00ffb37732c576122ceeddfa9ba3d7235ea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:53:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Rank shared hub slots across boards; queue line
 counts other boards' cards

Root cause: kanban.max_in_progress caps the host, but the gateway dispatcher
ticked boards one after another in a rotating order (_fair_board_order) and
each board's dispatch_once took every free slot for its own ready cards
(_tick_spawn_budget: remaining = cap - running on all boards). A freed slot
therefore went to whichever board ticked first, not to the best card. On
hermes-hub 2026-11-12 board `hermes` started two priority-0 cards at
05:08:50/52 while default-board t_01a1ac912db0cb5c (priority 51010, effective
1000) sat ready from 04:40 reading "0 card(s) ahead of it, 9/9 worker slots
busy": _ahead counted one board only.

Fix (hermes_cli/kanban_board_share.py):
- When free slots are fewer than the dispatchable cards on all boards, rank
  every board's ready/review candidates in DISPATCH_ORDER and give each board
  a spawn quota (dispatch_once spawn_quota); boards with a quota tick first,
  an unspent quota passes on. No contention = old behaviour.
- Starvation guard: a board whose top card has been ready >= 2 h takes the
  first pick (oldest first), so one board's flood of high priorities cannot
  hold another board forever.
- Queue position adds ahead_other_boards; the queue line and the 30-min
  nudge read "N card(s) ahead of it (M on other boards sharing these slots)".
- count_running_tasks_other_boards moves to the new module (re-exported) to
  keep kanban_db_dispatch.py under its line cap.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_kanban_cross_board_slots.py (two boards, one shared
slot: high card on the later board starts; flood vs starved board; queue
text; quota refusal text; plan ranking).
